# The published images a deployment pins to.
#
# Written by .github/workflows/publish-images.yml when a release is cut. Edit
# the workflow, not this file — a release overwrites it.
#
#   docker compose --env-file deploy/images.env up
#
# Each reference a release writes is a digest rather than a tag. A tag can be
# moved to point at different bytes; a digest is those bytes. Dependencies
# resolve at image build time and the base image tag moves, so one commit can
# yield materially different images — the commit says which source, the digest
# says which artefact, and only the digest is unambiguous.
#
# NOTHING IS PINNED YET. No release has been cut since image publication
# landed, so there is no digest to record and the two variables below are
# commented out rather than guessed. A deployment reading this file therefore
# pins nothing and compose falls back to its own default, which is the honest
# outcome — a reference written here before a release would name an image that
# does not exist. The first release replaces this block with real values.
#
# WOMBLEX_IMAGE_RELEASE=v0.0.0
# WOMBLEX_IMAGE_COMMIT=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
# WOMBLEX_PIPELINE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/deepcivic/womblex@sha256:...
# WOMBLEX_CONSOLE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/deepcivic/womblex-console@sha256:...
